<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Democratic Labour Party (Barbados)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Democratic Labour Party is a political party of Barbados, founded in 1955 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/errol-barrow">Errol Barrow</a> and other dissidents from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grantley-adams">Grantley Adams</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbados-labour-party">Barbados Labour Party</a>. It won the 1961 elections, and under Barrow led Barbados to independence on 30 November 1966. Since then it has alternated peacefully in government with the Barbados Labour Party.</p></div>
